ion polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tim Moore (R) is running."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's 14th District leans firmly Republican, and incumbent Tim Moore enters the general election with clear structural advantages. Moore has raised about $1.5 million and holds $1.6 million on hand, while Democrat Lakesha Womack has raised under $25,000 and reports negative cash. Womack also faces a pending felony charge that surfaced in court records and featured prominently in early-October coverage and the candidates' debate.\n\nRaters across the spectrum call the seat Safe or Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Moore roughly a 90 percent chance of holding it. The only public poll, a Republican-sponsored March survey of likely voters, showed Moore ahead by eight points, in line with the district's lean. Democrats' path runs through a strong national midterm environment and any traction from local coverage of candidates living outside the districts they seek to represent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0644, "margin": -9.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0543, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0528, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0536, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0567, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0477, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0569, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0517, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.061, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0542, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0382, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0377, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0552, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0